{"name":"Marsupilami","hex":"#fdf200","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Marsupilami","blocks":[{"text":"Marsupilami is a Belgian comic book character and fictional animal species created by Belgian comic artist André Franquin. Its first appearance was in the 31 January 1952 issue of the Franco-Belgian comics magazine Spirou. Since then it appeared regularly in the popular Belgian comics series Spirou & Fantasio, as a pet of the main characters, until Franquin stopped working on the series; the character's final appearance in the series during Franquin's lifetime was in 1970."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ef/Marsupilami_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsupilami","wikidata":"Q841812"},{"title":"Marsupilami (1993 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Marsupilami is a half-hour American animated television segment series that first appeared on television as short series that aired in the 1992 program Raw Toonage, and was then spun off into his own eponymous show on CBS for the 1993 season. The show was based on the character from the popular comic book by Belgian artist André Franquin et al."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e8/Marsupilami_title.jpg/330px-Marsupilami_title.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsupilami_(1993_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q3224333"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Marsupilaminest.JPG/500px-Marsupilaminest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Marsupilaminest.JPG/1280px-Marsupilaminest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Marsupilaminest.JPG/500px-Marsupilaminest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wall painting in Brussels, Belgium, depicting the Marsupilami family from Le nid des Marsupilamis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarsupilaminest.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Spirou_et_les_hommes-bulles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Spirou_et_les_hommes-bulles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Spirou et les hommes-bulles, 1959, by Franquin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpirou_et_les_hommes-bulles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Marsupilami_24_Operation_Attila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Marsupilami_24_Operation_Attila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Opération Attila, 2011. Art by Batem, story by Colman.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarsupilami_24_Operation_Attila.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG/500px-Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG/1280px-Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG/500px-Blondie_en_Blinkie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Blondin et Cirage wall painting featuring Jijé's Marsupilamus africanus character, in Brussels, Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlondie_en_Blinkie.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wi